From 7295f6239d7c818a81d13355aff472d27562ae26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kodi: the trim pass of the pictures mapped to the display
 follows "leave out the trims", and the log names the pass used

The mapping of Dolby Vision to the display's peak (Low-Latency, the HDR10 and SDR
outputs) applies the level 2 trim pass of the metadata where a block is for the
display's peak (dvbridge_hdr10_mapping::trims). It is on unless "Dolby Vision:
leave out the trims" (videoscreen.hadesdvnotrims) is on, the setting that already
decides whether a native output sends them; its help says so now (English, and
the Spanish of Estuary's strings). The two mappings take it with them, so that a
change of the setting starts a new mapping.

kodi.log says, once for a stream and from its first picture that has them, which
block was used (its target, the five values and their codes, the targets of the
stream's blocks), or that a block of the display's target is all neutral, or that
there are level 2 blocks and none for the display's peak, or that the pass could
not be drawn on the GPU and the stream goes on without it.
